{"slug": "one-pot-rice-and-quinoa", "nyt_id": 787679162, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/787679162-one-pot-rice-and-quinoa", "name": "One-Pot Rice and Quinoa", "author": "Ali Slagle", "description": "When you add quinoa to your pot of white rice, the grains end up every bit as fluffy and comforting, but with a lighter, bouncier texture, and an added helping of protein and fiber. Use this mix anytime you might plain white rice: in salads, with stir-fries or as a simple side. Be sure to check the package of quinoa to see if it’s been pre-washed; if it hasn’t, before cooking rinse it twice and shake it dry to remove its naturally occurring bitter, soapy coating.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings (about 6 cups)", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 5, "cook_minutes": 35, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 min", "prep": "PT0H5M", "cook": "PT0H35M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 cups water or broth", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water or broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup long-grain white rice, such as jasmine or basmati (no need to rinse)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "long-grain white rice", "preparation": "such as jasmine or basmati (no need to rinse)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 cup quinoa (any color)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "quinoa (any color)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Kosher salt (such as Diamond Crystal)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt (such as diamond crystal)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a large pot, bring the water to a boil. Add the rice, quinoa and 1 teaspoon kosher salt. Cover, reduce heat to low, and cook until the grains